# Never run the prod DB (hard)

Do **not** run, trigger, or “helpfully” execute anything against production / Neon. Not to unblock seed, not to verify a fix, not because a script failed, not because the user looks busy. **No exception. No workaround.**

The user runs prod. You may print the command for them to copy.

## Forbidden

- `pnpm db:prod` and any other `*:prod` / `db:*:prod` script
- `DOTENV_CONFIG_PATH` or any load aimed at `apps/api/.env` (Neon)
- `psql` / `drizzle-kit` / `tsx` against the prod `DATABASE_URL`
- Migrate, seed, or ad-hoc SQL on prod

```text
# ❌ BAD — agent runs this
pnpm db:prod

# ✅ GOOD — tell the user; stop
You run: pnpm db:prod
```

Local `.env.local` scripts (`pnpm db:migrate`, `pnpm db:seed`) stay allowed unless the user said otherwise.

If a task seems to need prod: **stop**, say you will not touch prod, give the exact command. Do not run it.
